# Ansel: on the rail, then ashore with Rook.
dialogue ansel4
  node root ansel "Son! I'd come down, but they say I'm contagious. I feel wonderful. That's a symptom, apparently."
    > "Rook's in the Salty Keel." if (met_rook or seen:rook4.root) and not seen:ansel.rook and not seen:ansel4.rook -> rook
    > "Cray will write you down as lost again." -> again
    > "How are the crews?" if not seen:ansel4.crews -> crews
    > "Goodnight, Father." -> night
  node rook ansel "Rook! Tell him he owes me a reef. No, wait. Tell him I'm glad. Then tell him about the reef."
  node again ansel "Again? He'll wear the page out. He can argue with my log. It's mostly weather. But the weather was him."
  node crews ansel "A hundred and thirty sailors can see their front doors. Nobody sleeps. Tam Hobb tried to swim for it. His brother sat on him."
  node night ansel "Goodnight, son. Mind the third plank on the pier. Loose for years. I keep meaning to report it. To you, now."
  # Ashore, at Rook's table, after the quarantine's lifted.
  node ashore ansel "Son! Rook owes me a reef, and he's paying in rum. It isn't legal tender. I'm not proud."
    > "What will you do now?" if not seen:ansel4.shop -> shop
    > "Should I sail with the Marrow?" if not seen:ansel4.point -> point
    > "(Leave them to it.)" -> leave
  node shop ansel "A shop. Compasses that point at the Old Nail. Useless anywhere else. I'll sell them to people who want to come home."
  node point ansel "I sailed twenty years. My best navigating was leaving a compass on a hall table. Don't ask me where to point."
    -> stake
  node stake ansel "You've seen what I do at the third stake."
  node leave rook "Go on, boy. Your captain and I have three years of lying to catch up on."
